Z||000000||CoolBlue87GT||11-21-2001||09:42 AM||||This lift was in the post 'Dream Garage' in General Chat<P>Anyone know about these floor lifts ?<P>It looks portable.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/delgarage1.jpg">  <P>I want one !!<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||grinthock||11-21-2001||09:50 AM||||Never seen it!<P>Actually this is a good time to ask.<P>Who here HAS a lift?   I am building a garage in the spring and I am looking for inexpensive lift's.  Must be able to lift fullsize CARS, Ford Taurus sized vehicles.<P>Options?  Prices... Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000002||Patrick's Dad||11-21-2001||10:43 AM||||I don't know whose that one is, in particular, but Snap-On has one of that design. It is portable, although, I would expect, quite heavy. It is designed to roll under the car, then lift it.<P>I have seen these in Hot Rod magazine, too.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Lou Christopher||11-21-2001||10:48 AM||||I recently bought a Ben Pack drive on lift.  $ 2500 delivered.  Took myself and a friend about 10 hours to install.  I have had it for a year now and no proplems.  I also bought from them a rolling piece which goes between the ramps.  I use a bottle jack to raise the wheels off  when necessary.  The advantage of the ramp lift is you do not need the depth and strength of concrete required for a frame lift and you get on and off without crawling under the car to position arms.<BR>                        Lou||||reg||1
Z||000004||FormulaJoe||11-21-2001||12:50 PM||||I have seen those lifts before at Sams Club in their tire department.  They are designed to lift a car enough to change the tires (12-18 inch, not much more) since there is all the lift mechanism under there.  Would be nice to have for working on suspension, brakes and tire/wheels.  As someone posted earlier check out some of the car magazines they have advertisements for such things.  On a normal car they lift them by the sides, but on a Fiero thats not a good idea.  May want to try one before buying, if you can find one locally.<P>------------------<BR>Yellow Formula<BR>(soon to be 3.4 DOHC)||||reg||6
Z||000005||Fierobruiser||11-21-2001||10:48 PM||||Check out this site. The style my mechanic used when dropping the engine for a clutch replacement was the TP-9 @ $2239.00. It leaves the back end open when lifting the car off the cradle assembly. <A HREF="http://www.lifts.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.lifts.com/</A> <P>------------------<BR>Notchbacks Rule<BR>85GT(show car)<BR>88Coupe (daily driver)<BR>84 Coupe(project car)||||reg||1
Z||000006||GT GT 87||11-22-2001||12:08 AM||||In the front of Hemmings Motor News  there are at least 8-10 ads for lifts . Most are made to also park a car under it for added storage of a classic car .......||||reg||1
